    "html": "<p>Two radio transmitters, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>, emit coherent waves of wavelength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda\"></span> in phase with each other. At a certain distance from the transmitters, the path difference to a receiver is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\lambda}{8}\"></span>. What is the phase difference between the two waves when they reach the receiver?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\pi}{8} \\text{ rad}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\text{ rad}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\text{ rad}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\pi \\text{ rad}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
